# .percolate-ignore — coordinator_core/ contributing source root for the
# claude-klabauter OSS mirror (row 1 of the three publish rows authored in
# docs/plans/2026-07-31-claude-klabauter-oss-release.md § C5).
#
# SOURCE_DIR for this file is `claude-klabauter/coordinator_core/` itself.
# Patterns are SOURCE_DIR-RELATIVE — they carry NO `coordinator_core/`
# prefix, or they double-prefix to `coordinator_core/coordinator_core/…`
# and match nothing (same trap the sibling `coordinator/.percolate-ignore`
# warns about in its own header).
#
# PM RULING (2026-07-31-claude-klabauter-oss-release.md § C3, "settled, do
# not re-argue"): `coordinator_core/**` INCLUDING ITS TEST SUITE SHIPS — the
# 2045 test files are the artifact's main credibility signal. Do NOT add
# `tests/` or `fixtures/` exclusions here the way the sibling
# `coordinator/.percolate-ignore` does for the bin/lib row: that file's
# rationale (dev-only tests should never reach a doctrine-only mirror) does
# not apply to an engine mirror that is explicitly publishing its own test
# suite as proof of correctness.
#
# MECHANISM — READ BEFORE ADDING A PATTERN HERE. Row 1 is SINGLE-SOURCE
# (contributing_roots == {coordinator_core/} only, so
# `build_allowlisted_source`'s multi-source branch never fires — see
# coordinator/lib/percolate/allowlist.py:377-395,
# `build_allowlisted_source`). In single-source mode
# `build_allowlisted_source` does NOT build a copy-time `ignore_fn`
# (allowlist.py:426-432, `build_allowlisted_source`: `ignore_fn = None`
# unless multi_source) — this file is only copied verbatim into the
# restricted temp tree (allowlist.py:468-474, same function), never
# consulted while that tree is assembled. It becomes live one stage later,
# when coordinator/bin/publish.py's `dispatch_mirror_like`
# (publish.py:1772-1815) loads it (publish.py:1790-1791) and hands it to
# DoE-claude's `setup/publish_sync.py::sync_mirror`, which consults it
# symmetrically on BOTH the copy phase (Phase 1, `ignore.matches(...)` at
# publish_sync.py:512) and the destination delete phase (Phase 2,
# `ignore.matches(...)` at publish_sync.py:537) — an ignored file is neither
# copied nor deleted on either leg.
#
# This file has NO effect on the earlier `check_working_data_paths`
# secondary-assertion gate (allowlist.py:482-554, invoked from
# `run_pre_sync_gates` in publish.py:1352-1358), which scans the raw,
# unfiltered restricted tree BEFORE this file is ever read for filtering
# purposes. That gate is confirmed (2026-07-31, this chunk's run report) to
# hard-fail row 1 as currently allowlisted: several
# `*/tests/fixtures/.../{state,docs/plans,cross-repo,archive}/...` paths
# under coordinator_core/benchmarks, coordinator_core/ops/ceremony, and
# coordinator_core/ops/emit exist purely as test fixtures but contain
# deny-listed path segments, and `check_working_data_paths`'s any-depth
# substring match (`f"/{prefix}/" in rel`) cannot distinguish them from real
# working data. See this chunk's run-report sidecar for the full violation
# list. Fixing that is an allowlist/check_working_data_paths-shape decision,
# not a `.percolate-ignore` one — out of this file's reach by construction.
#
# SUPERSEDED (2026-08-12, docs/plans/2026-08-12-publish-allowlist-acknowledges-
# imported-modules.md § C3): the hard-fail claim above is no longer current.
# Row 1's field 7 in `setup/publish-targets.portable` has since gained three
# `!`-exclusions — `!benchmarks/fixtures/repo`,
# `!ops/ceremony/tests/fixtures/render_handoff_tracker`, and
# `!ops/emit/tests/fixtures/root` — which between them account for all 40
# deny-prefix hits under coordinator_core that the gate was flagging.
# Re-measured 2026-08-12: `check_working_data_paths(tmp,
# paths=get_pre_filter_paths(tmp))` on the current row-1 allowlist returns
# `True` ("no working-data paths in publish set"). The gate is green as of
# this writing; treat the paragraph above as historical record of a
# now-resolved state, not a live blocker.

# --- Python build artifacts ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/

# --- Editor / OS detritus ---
*.bak
*.tmp
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.orig
*.rej
